        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "Corroboration does not mean treating the narrator like a suspect. It means building a richer evidence field. Compare dates and names with club minutes, newspapers, photographs, directories, policy documents, and other interviews. When sources conflict, record the difference and ask what each source was positioned to know. A club record may document an official decision; an interview may reveal how that decision felt, who was excluded, or how community members adapted. Neither source automatically cancels the other."
        },
