          "text": "An oral-history interview is not a transparent window into the past. It is a historical source created in a particular encounter. The narrator chooses what to remember and how to tell it; the interviewer shapes the path through questions and reactions; the recording medium and archive shape what later audiences can access. Begin with the source itself: who participated, when and where it was recorded, what language or languages were used, what the project asked about, and what permissions govern use."
